  "comments": [
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "73cd98fa_7ff3d15b",
        "filename": "chip/g/usb-stream.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 138,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-20T16:34:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have an alternative suggestion, let\u0027s use this flag to indicate that USB transmitter is not yet idle. It would be set when data is added to the queue and cleared when there is no more data to queue.\n\nSo, no need to clear it here.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 137,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 138,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "355fb38c1e979ae7d8b6ac29420a60960372a8c6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "39facbcd_71d19d86",
        "filename": "chip/g/usb-stream.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 138,
      "author": {
        "id": 1283719
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-20T18:03:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is a case that usb_written() is not used. I am planning to apply USB stream on usb_console.c which has null queue consumer policy. Console_task will call tx_stream_handler directly.\n\nThis check should be in tx_stream_handler(), and the variable should play a lock role to keep this function atomic-ish.",
      "parentUuid": "73cd98fa_7ff3d15b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 137,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 138,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "355fb38c1e979ae7d8b6ac29420a60960372a8c6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cc420609_db66baf1",
        "filename": "chip/g/usb-stream.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 138,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-20T18:27:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "we can reason about switching console to streaming when implementation comes along, the point now is that this flag, whatever we call it, should indicate if the supplier of bytes has to call tx_stream_handler() or not.",
      "parentUuid": "39facbcd_71d19d86",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 137,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 138,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "355fb38c1e979ae7d8b6ac29420a60960372a8c6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6d7ec978_b090b113",
        "filename": "chip/g/usb-stream.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 138,
      "author": {
        "id": 1283719
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-20T19:21:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "tx_fifo_is_ready() is playing that kind of indication role already. But, there are time gaps between line 141 and 198. I think the lock to keep those area atomic.",
      "parentUuid": "cc420609_db66baf1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 137,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 138,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "355fb38c1e979ae7d8b6ac29420a60960372a8c6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b09c4ceb_8f795b2e",
        "filename": "chip/g/usb-stream.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 141,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-20T16:34:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this check should be in usb_written(), this is the only place which can be called asynchronously (even though currently it is running in interrupt context).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 141,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 141,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "355fb38c1e979ae7d8b6ac29420a60960372a8c6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "caf316a8_b8f45ffe",
        "filename": "chip/g/usb-stream.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 141,
      "author": {
        "id": 1283719
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-20T18:03:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "tx_fifo_is_ready() should be called here.\nLet\u0027s assume that hook_task was resetting USB:\nhook_task() -\u003e line 247                                                      line 248\n                       ^                                                     ^\n                       |                                                     |\n                       UART IRQ Handler-\u003eusb_written() -\u003e tx_stream_handler() \n\nIt was about to run line 248, but UART interrupt handler was triggered and added data. Eventually usb_written() called tx_stream_handler() and setup transfer. After that\nthe control came back to hook_task, and it called tx_stream_handler().\nIf tx_stream_handler() would call tx_fifo_is_ready(), then it would know that transfer was\non-going, and would return, not overwriting TX endpoint descriptor.",
      "parentUuid": "b09c4ceb_8f795b2e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 141,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 141,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "355fb38c1e979ae7d8b6ac29420a60960372a8c6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5c278107_cf857154",
        "filename": "chip/g/usb-stream.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 141,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-20T18:27:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "but before calling tx_stream_handler() usb_tx_in_progress would be set, so, usb_written() would not call tx_stream_handler()\n\nThis function will be called on every USB packet interrupt, we should keep it as light as possible.",
      "parentUuid": "caf316a8_b8f45ffe",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 141,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 141,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "355fb38c1e979ae7d8b6ac29420a60960372a8c6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fa9aab0f_59fd4dae",
        "filename": "chip/g/usb-stream.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 141,
      "author": {
        "id": 1283719
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-20T19:21:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, now I catch that in your suggestion, usb_tx_in_progress is zero initially, and usb_reset() will set it 1 (in line 245) to indicate that it is going to setup transfer. If UART got some data while usb_reset() has not been called, then usb_written() would proceed assuming tx is not in progress. At this time USB TX endpoint descriptors is not initialized. \n\nHowever, in ToT code, tx_fifo_is_ready() will say \"No\" if it sees the uninitialized status has \"DIEPDMA_BS_HOST_RDY (0x0 \u003c\u003c 30)\". Are we ok with this?",
      "parentUuid": "5c278107_cf857154",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 141,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 141,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "355fb38c1e979ae7d8b6ac29420a60960372a8c6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2e2207aa_6851a197",
        "filename": "chip/g/usb-stream.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 141,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-20T19:55:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e However, in ToT code, tx_fifo_is_ready() will say \"No\" if it sees the \n\u003e uninitialized status has \"DIEPDMA_BS_HOST_RDY (0x0 \u003c\u003c 30)\". Are we ok\n\u003e with this?\n\nI think so - this would mean that the descriptor has not yet been set up, right?",
      "parentUuid": "fa9aab0f_59fd4dae",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 141,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 141,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "355fb38c1e979ae7d8b6ac29420a60960372a8c6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
