    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "54126456_2071fc19",
        "filename": "chip/g/usb-stream.h",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 32,
      "author": {
        "id": 1283719
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-20T18:03:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The initial value, zero or false, should block any code enter into tx_stream_handler.\nI am renaming it as tx_ep_writable, which represents if TX endpoint can be writable or not.",
      "parentUuid": "d8ea51c3_844a0bb2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 32,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 32,
        "endChar": 12
      },
      "revId": "355fb38c1e979ae7d8b6ac29420a60960372a8c6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4c7f4aab_f9292ce8",
        "filename": "chip/g/usb-stream.h",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 32,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-20T18:27:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not sure tx_ep_writeable is as descriptive. Maybe \u0027tx_not_idle\u0027 is a better name if you don\u0027t like \u0027tx_in_progress\u0027",
      "parentUuid": "54126456_2071fc19",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 32,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 32,
        "endChar": 12
      },
      "revId": "355fb38c1e979ae7d8b6ac29420a60960372a8c6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4136e25a_d6935f6d",
        "filename": "chip/g/usb-stream.h",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 32,
      "author": {
        "id": 1283719
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-20T19:21:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the zero value should also indicate that \u0027endpoint is uninitialized\u0027, like \u0027is_reset\u0027 in ToT. I believe that this check should be in tx_stream_handler.\n\nThe status of USB endpoint descriptor is playing a lock role and represents the transfer status, and I intended this variable to be a lock for USB endpoint descriptor status.",
      "parentUuid": "4c7f4aab_f9292ce8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 32,
        "startChar": 1,
